==Description==

The [[Image:Assembly_CreateJointRigidGroup.svg|24px]] [[Assembly_CreateJointRigidGroup|Assembly CreateJointRigidGroup]] tool creates a rigid group that permanently locks the selected components together.

==Usage==

# Make sure that an assembly is active.
# Select components to be grouped.
# There are several ways to invoke the tool:
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:Assembly_CreateJointRigidGroup.svg|16px]] [[Assembly_CreateJointRigidGroup|Create Rigid Group]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Assembly → [[Image:Assembly_CreateJointRigidGroup.svg|16px]] Create Rigid Group}} option from the menu.
#* Use the keyboard shortcut: {{KEY|O}}.
# A '''RigidGroupJoint''' object is added to the Joints container.

==Notes==

RigidGroupJoint objects are permanently inactive (grayed out) ignoring the Visibility property.

==Properties==

See also: [[Property_View|Property View]].

A '''RigidGroupJoint''' object is derived from an [[App_FeaturePython|App FeaturePython]] object and inherits all its properties. It also has the following additional properties:

====Data====

{{Properties_Title|Rigid Group}}

* {{PropertyData|Objects To Rigid Group|LinkList}}: List of references to components to group together.
* {{PropertyData|Rigid Placements|PlacementList}}: Relative placements for restore.


